Hi people,

I have a kind request about the license of libiptc. Before I continue, 
'no' is also a very acceptable response, so please don't start an 
unnecessary flame war. (I know how religious a discussion like this can 
be) :-)

We are currently using libiptc in our (not yet released) product to 
access functionality that is not accessible through the iptables 
command. During a license/code review I noticed that the license of 
libiptc is GPL instead of LGPL. As we are not yet in the position to 
release our code this is a problem for us.

So my request is if the iptables team would consider a license change 
that is in favor of 3rd party developers like ourself who wish to 
integrate iptables in their products.

  S.
